// NEGATIVE TEST -- a nested array struct FIELD whose inner length is a const
// generic is refused (N4-10).
//
// The sibling of tests/reject/nested_array_param_inner_length.pd, one
// declaration position over, and it needs its own fixture because the two
// positions build their declarators in two different places: a parameter in
// `array_param_declarator`, a field in `generate_struct`. The reason is the
// same and it is C's: every dimension after the first decides a stride, so a
// length this compiler cannot resolve has no honest spelling there.
//
// Unlike the parameter, a field is not merely uncallable -- there is no
// program at all that can name this struct's shape, because the length does
// not exist. It is refused at the declaration rather than at some later use,
// which is where a reader can still see the `N` they wrote.
struct Board {
    cells: [[i64; N]; 2],
}

fn main() {
    print_int(1);
}
